  "steps" : [ "Adjust oven rack to middle position and heat oven to 325 degrees. Grease a 13 by 9-inch baking dish. Combine sour cream, mayonnaise, almonds, cheddar, Gruyère, onion, celery, lemon juice, chives, salt, and cayenne in a large bowl. Fold in chicken until thoroughly combined. Transfer mixture to prepared dish and spread in an even layer.", "Place potato chips and paprika in a large zipper-lock bag, press to remove air, and seal. Using a rolling pin, crush chips to fine crumbs. Sprinkle chip mixture evenly over casserole. Bake until casserole is bubbling and chips begin to brown, 40 to 45 minutes. Let cool for 10 minutes and serve." ],
