  "notes" : "This take on a classic Thai stir-fry is not for those with timid palates. Pork tenderloin is easier to slice if it is partially frozen. Freeze until firm but not frozen solid, 45 minutes to 1 hour, then cut into 1/4-inch slices, and further into 1/4-inch strips. The marination and quick stir-frying keep the pork tender and seasoned. Vegetables are batch-cooked due to differing cook times, with aromatics added at the end. Chicken broth adds depth, and cornstarch thickens the sauce slightly to coat the ingredients.",
